hether you'd like to schedule it manually after project creation.  See Creating a Custom Code Analysis Project.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-11-15\nValid as Of: 2024-11-15\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2411\n\n--- Record 1924 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: Display Business Event Logs\nDescription: The app is part of Business Event Logging. It provides an overview of logged business events for different objects and event types. You can explore the details of the event with this app.  For more information, see Display Business Event Logs.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-10-10\nValid as Of: 2024-11-15\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2411\n\n--- Record 1925 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: Display Business Events by Objects\nDescription: The app is part of Business Event Logging. It groups business events by instances of objects and object components. You can discover the processing sequences with this app.   For more information, see Display Business Events by Objects.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-10-10\nValid as Of: 2024-11-15\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2411\n\n--- Record 1926 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: Display Changes to Objects\nDescription: The app is part of Business Event Logging. You can see the changes for your objects on a field level as recorded in business event logging.  For more information, see Display Changes to Objects.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-10-10\nValid as Of: 2024-11-15\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2411\n\n--- Record 1927 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: New Parameters To Request Cloning A BYOG Repository\nDescription: When cloning a software component, you can now optionally use the newly added parameters to request cloning a Bring Your Own Git (BYOG) repository.  For more information, see Bring Your Own Git.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-10-15\nValid as Of: 2024-11-15\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2411\n\n--- Record 1928 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: Referenced SAPUI5 Version\nDescription: As part of hotfix collection 3, SAPUI5 version 1.127.5 is used for the administrator’s SAP Fiori launchpad, SAP-delivered Fiori apps, and the custom-built SAP Fiori apps, which are deployed to the ABAP system.  See SAP BTP ABAP Environment – Maintenance Windows and Major Upgrade Windows in 2024 and SAP UI5\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-08-06\nValid as Of: 2024-11-15\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2411\n\n--- Record 1929 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: Security Incident and Event Management API for Read Access Logs\nDescription: The communication scenario SAP_COM_0915 provides access to APIs to read the Read Access Logs from the system. The API can for instance be leveraged by a Security Incident and Event Management (SIEM) system.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-11-15\nValid as Of: 2024-11-15\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2411\n\n--- Record 1930 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: Support of Launchpad App Descriptor Items", ". The API can for instance be leveraged by a Security Incident and Event Management (SIEM) system.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-11-15\nValid as Of: 2024-11-15\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2411\n\n--- Record 1930 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: Support of Launchpad App Descriptor Items in ABAP Development Tools for Eclipse\nDescription: You can now create and maintain launchpad app descriptor items in ABAP development tools for Eclipse. These items describe how an application is started and consist of a target mapping and one or more tiles.  For more information, see SAP Fiori Applications in the ABAP Environment and Working with Launchpad App Descriptor Items.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-10-15\nValid as Of: 2024-11-15\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2411\n\n", "--- Record 411 ---\nComponent: SAP BTP, Cloud Foundry Runtime\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Version 50.1.0\nDescription: Cloud Foundry has been updated from 49.4.0 to 50.1.0.    https://github.com/cloudfoundry/cf-deployment/releases/tag/v50.1.0  https://github.com/cloudfoundry/cf-deployment/releases/tag/v50.0.0  https://github.com/cloudfoundry/cf-deployment/releases/tag/v49.5.0  \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-07-24\nValid as Of: 2025-07-24\nVersion: 2507a\n\n--- Record 412 ---\nComponent: Application for Data Replication and Administration\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: New Version Indicator in Getting Support\nDescription: A new version indicator has been added to the screen Getting Support, that means that the version 2508 will be shown for services that are running on this version. Please note that there are two release dates for configuration and pricing services.   See Release Schedule and Dates and Getting Support.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-07-08\nValid as Of: 2025-07-23\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 413 ---\nComponent: Cloud Portal Service\nEnvironment: Neo\nTitle: Change in Deployment Timeline\nDescription: Starting from 2507A release (22-23.7.25), the release to production will shift one day earlier and will take place, in most cases, on Tuesdays & Wednesdays every other week.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Announcement\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-06-26\nValid as Of: 2025-07-23\nVersion: 2507A\n\n--- Record 414 ---\nComponent: Cloud Portal Service\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Change in Deployment Timeline\nDescription: Starting from 2507A release (22-23.7.25), the release to production will shift one day earlier and will take place, in most cases, on Tuesdays & Wednesdays every other week.   For more information about the planned timeline, please refer to the SAP Note: 3303878 - Release schedule for SAP Build Work Zone. \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Announcement\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-06-26\nValid as Of: 2025-07-23\nVersion: 2507A\n\n--- Record 415 ---\nComponent: Cloud Transport Management\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Data protection and privacy information of the service can now be accessed directly from the UI of the service.\nDescription: From the User Profile dropdown menu, you can now directly open the data protection and privacy information in the SAP Cloud Transport Management documentation on SAP Help Portal.  See:   SAP Cloud Transport Management Home Screen. In the topic, select the Title Bar, and then scroll down to the User Profile section.  \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Announcement\nLine of Business: Application Development and Integration\nLatest Revision: 2025-07-23\nValid as Of: 2025-07-23\nVersion: 2507a\n\n--- Record 416 ---\nComponent: Cloud Transport Management\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: UI changes\nDescription: Landscape Visualization:    Introduction of an overview graph for navigation in large transport landscapes, as well as options to adjust the orientation and placement of nodes.       Highlighting of transport nodes using icons and color to indicate the overall import status of a node and quick overview of important configuration settings.       Selecting a transport node or route now allows you to open a details popover.       Editing a node or route was moved from the icon bar to the popover.       See:   Using the Landscape Visualization  \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Announcement\nLine of Business: Application Development and Integration\nLatest Revision: 2025-07-23\nValid as Of: 2025-07-23\nVersion: 2507a\n\n--- Record 417 ---\nComponent: Pricing Service\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Pre-Production - Document Pricing – Do Not Lose Condition Values During Repricing\nDescription: If a price recalculation with type C (Carries out a new pricing, manually entered conditions are retained) was triggered, an automatically determined condition value used to get lost in the following case: The condition appeared twice in the results, one value with control flag A (Adjust for quantity variance) and origin flag A (Automatic pricing) and another value with control flag C (Changed manually) and origin flag C (Manually entered/changed). This issue has been corrected, which can lead to unexpected pricing results if the issue was unnoticed before.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-06-25\nValid as Of: 2025-07-23\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 418 ---\nComponent: Pricing Service\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Pre-Production - Support More Standard Pricing Routines\nDescription: There are some newly supported pricing requirement formulas:    11 No Material    20 Price Charge    28 No Variant (SA)    29 No Exception 'N'  30 No Exclusion 'V'  35 Plant Info Record  37 Variant  42 Pricing – Normal  57 Not Free Goods w/o", "\n\n--- Record 418 ---\nComponent: Pricing Service\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Pre-Production - Support More Standard Pricing Routines\nDescription: There are some newly supported pricing requirement formulas:    11 No Material    20 Price Charge    28 No Variant (SA)    29 No Exception 'N'  30 No Exclusion 'V'  35 Plant Info Record  37 Variant  42 Pricing – Normal  57 Not Free Goods w/o return item    Newly supported pricing base value formulas:  23 Preference  25 Cash Discount  44 VAT France  61 Preference  220 Gross Value    See: Supported Standard Pricing Exits.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-06-25\nValid as Of: 2025-07-23\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 419 ---\nComponent: Pricing Service\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Pre-Production – Size Limit for Price Determination Trace\nDescription: Pricing service will stop writing pricing determination traces when an estimated memory size of about 5MB is reached. That should be sufficient for most cases. When the limit is reached, a corresponding info message is added to the trace. SAP can optimize this size limit for support cases and can additionally limit the pricing determination trace to a list of relevant condition types.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-06-25\nValid as Of: 2025-07-23\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 420 ---\nComponent: SAP Build Process Automation\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Monitoring Guided Process\nDescription: You can view and monitor Guided Process instances in the Process and Workflow Instances tile in the Monitoring section.See Process and Workflow Instances. \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-07-23\nValid as Of: 2025-07-23\nVersion: Cloud\n\n", "--- Record 681 ---\nComponent: Cloud Integration\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Migration Tooling Limitations\nDescription: Now, extensions are imported automatically during the migration of integration objects from your on-premise