d Transport Management with Other SAP Cloud Solutions  Tutorial: Transport Mobile Development Kit (MDK) apps using SAP Content Agent UI  \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Announcement\nLine of Business: Application Development and Integration\nLatest Revision: 2025-06-06\nValid as Of: 2025-06-06\nVersion: Cloud\n\n", "--- Record 591 ---\nComponent: SAP Document AI\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: New Improved ML Model for Purchase Order\nDescription: We’ve improved the machine learning model for purchase order documents.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Intelligent Technologies\nLatest Revision: 2025-06-27\nValid as Of: 2025-06-24\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 592 ---\nComponent: SAP Document AI\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Overall Improvements\nDescription: There have been several code and stability improvements.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Intelligent Technologies\nLatest Revision: 2025-06-27\nValid as Of: 2025-06-24\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 593 ---\nComponent: SAP HANA Cloud\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry,Kyma,Other\nTitle: New component version available\nDescription: A new component version is available for the following SAP HANA Cloud components:   2025.14 (QRC 2/2025) for SAP HANA Cloud, SAP HANA database  2025.2.5816 (QRC 2/2025) for SAP HANA Cloud, data lake      See What's New in SAP HANA Cloud.  Action: To use the new component version, you must upgrade your instance. See Managing SAP HANA Cloud Instances.\nAction: Recommended\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-06-23\nValid as Of: 2025-06-23\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 594 ---\nComponent: Cloud Identity Services\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry,Kyma,Neo\nTitle: Off-Cycle Upgrade\nDescription: Cloud Identity Services have been upgraded.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-06-23\nValid as Of: 2025-06-23\nVersion: 27990\n\n--- Record 595 ---\nComponent: Cloud Identity Services\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry,Kyma,Neo\nTitle: Signing Certificates\nDescription: As of June 23, 2025 the version of the newly created signing certificates is v3. See Tenant SAML 2.0 Configurations.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Announcement\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-06-23\nValid as Of: 2025-06-23\nVersion: 27990\n\n--- Record 596 ---\nComponent: Process Visibility Capability\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Configure Navigation Link on Steps\nDescription: You can now configure navigation link on steps to navigate to specific pages for additional details.  See Configure Step Navigation Link.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-06-23\nValid as Of: 2025-06-23\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 597 ---\nComponent: SAP AI Core\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Generative AI hub\nDescription: Prompt shields are available as part of input filtering with Azure Content Safety. Prompt shields detect and mitigate prompt attacks, such as prompts designed to bypass safety mechanisms or override previous instruction. For more information, see Harm categories in Azure AI Content Safety and Input Filtering.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Announcement\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-06-23\nValid as Of: 2025-06-23\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 598 ---\nComponent: SAP AI Core\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Generative AI hub\nDescription: We now support the Anthropic models Claude Opus 4 and Claude Sonnet 4.  For more information, see SAP Note 3437766 .\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Announcement\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-06-23\nValid as Of: 2025-06-23\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 599 ---\nComponent: SAP AI Launchpad\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Generative AI hub\nDescription: We now support the Anthropic models Claude Opus 4 and Claude Sonnet 4.  For more information, see SAP Note 3437766 .\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Announcement\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-06-23\nValid as Of: 2025-06-23\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 600 ---\nComponent: SAP Build\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: New Copy Feature for Actions Project\nDescription: You can now duplicate and reuse actions within your project using the new Copy feature. This helps you save time and maintain consistency across similar projects.  See Copy Actions.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-06-23\nValid as Of: 2025-06-23\nVersion: Cloud\n\n", "--- Record 3001 ---\nComponent: Pricing Service\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Extension Concept - Provide More Data to Requirement Implementations\nDescription: The pricing engine used to only pass parameters attributes and exclusioIndicator as input data to requirement implementations.  This is still the default behavior, but through a projection on fields of structure itemInput in COLLECT ATTRIBUTES' response via extendedInput>documentInput>itemInput>projection it is now also possible to request the item quantity and other conditions information for a requirement formula.  For a requirement formula, it is only possible to retrieve a subset of the conditions field for the already determined pricing conditions:    stepNumber      counter      conditionType      conditionRate      conditionUnit      scale      See API Definition and Extension Guide for SAP Variant Configuration and Pricing.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-03-25\nValid as Of: 2024-05-02\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3002 ---\nComponent: Pricing Service\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Pricing Engine Trace - Log Inactivity Because of a Missing Routine Implementation\nDescription: When a pricing implementation is missing, the condition type will be marked as inactive in the pricing results. But in the calculation trace, the reason for the inactivity used to be missing. This issue has been corrected.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-03-25\nValid as Of: 2024-05-02\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3003 ---\nComponent: Pricing Service\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: SAP Cloud ALM Integration for Performance Monitoring\nDescription: The Real User Monitoring start page, which should provide an overview of all service requests, was hard to read because a very large number of individual requests was listed. This happened due to some IDs in the paths of the requests that could not be aggregated at the endpoint level. This issue has been corrected by replacing such IDs with an asterisk. With that, now you see aggregations such as /api/v1/pricing/documents/*/conditions/* or /api/v1/pricing/documents/*/items/* instead of individual requests per document id, item id, or condition id.  See Administration Guide for SAP Variant Configuration and Pricing.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-04-15\nValid as Of: 2024-05-02\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3004 ---\nComponent: Pricing Service\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Stateless Pricing - Enable SAP CPQ to Work With Alternative Units of Measure\nDescription: In pricing results, the condition rates are returned as maintained. Only condition values are returned in the target document currency based on the item’s target quantity and unit of measure. To help SAP CPQ to cope with condition rates that use alternative units of measure, the item condition details of endpoint POST /api/v1/statelesspricing is enhanced with a new field conditionRateNormalized, which also considers the target currency and the sales unit of measure.   This field is for use in SAP CPQ only and may change becoming incompatible at any time when requested by SAP CPQ. Do not use this field in any other integrations.  See API Definition and Development Guide for SAP Variant Configuration and Pricing.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-03-25\nValid as Of: 2024-05-02\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3005 ---\nComponent: Pricing Service\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Support Custom Subtotal Flags\nDescription: Custom subtotal flags in a pricing procedure used to cause an error. This issue has been corrected.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-03-25\nValid as Of: 2024-05-02\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3006 ---\nComponent: Pricing Service\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Support Data Determination Access Type C - KOMPAZAD\nDescription: Data determination at condition access level was previously not supported by the Pricing service. This also meant that the Pricing service did not consider condition record fields with access type C Data Field from Condition Table  This gap has been closed. The Pricing service supports the determination of fields in the structure KOMPAZD in an access and their use for the condition determination in a subsequent access.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-03-25\nValid as Of: 2024-05-02\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3007 ---\nComponent: SAP Build Process Automation\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Manage and Monitor your Events\nDescription: You can now connect your events at one place, to manage, monitor, and to ensure they run smoothly.For more information, see Connect with SAP Integration Suite, Advanced Event Mesh.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-05-02\nValid as Of: 2024-05-02\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3008 ---\nComponent: SAP HANA Service\nEnvironment: Neo\nTitle: Monitoring of SAP HANA Tenant Databases Unused Memory\nDescription: On the Monitoring view of your database systems, you can now view the HANA Tenant Databases Unused Memory metric to monitor the unused memory. See View Memory Usage for an SAP HANA Database System.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General", "05-02\nValid as Of: 2024-05-02\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3008 ---\nComponent: SAP HANA Service\nEnvironment: Neo\nTitle: Monitoring of SAP HANA Tenant Databases Unused Memory\nDescription: On the Monitoring view of your database systems, you can now view the HANA Tenant Databases Unused Memory metric to monitor the unused memory. See View Memory Usage for an SAP HANA Database System.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-05-02\nValid as Of: 2024-05-02\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3009 ---\nComponent: Data Quality Services\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry,Neo\nTitle: Enhancements\nDescription:   The microservice now supports address validation in Bolivia to the street level and sometimes to the house number level. See Country Coverage for more information.   Improvements were made to type ahead suggestions when entering a United Kingdom postcode.   Migration from the Neo environment to Cloud Foundry is now available. For more information, see Migrating Data Quality Services from Neo to Cloud Foundry Environment.  Note  The Neo environment will be deprecated December 31, 2028.    \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Announcement\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-01-01\nValid as Of: 2024-05-01\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3010 ---\nComponent: Mobile Services\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Additional user interface languages\nDescription: (Version: 2404) The Mobile Services cockpit is now available in Serbian (Cyrillic), Serbian (Latin), Montenegrin, and Macedonian.Note  The documentation is still translated only in Simplified Chinese and Japanese.  See User Interface\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-04-16\nValid as Of: 2024-05-01\nVersion: Cloud\n\n", "--- Record 431 ---\nComponent: SAP Java Buildpack\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Version 2.35.1\nDescription: SAP Java Buildpack 2 has been updated from version 2.35.0 to 2.35.1. Updated components:       You can now profile SapMachine-based applications by using the async-profiler tool and cf CLI Java plugin. To learn how, see: Profile an Application Running on SapMachine with async-profiler      SapMachine 17 is updated from version 17.0.15 to 17.0.16      SapMachine 21 is updated from version 21.0.7 to 21.0.8    \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-07-18\nValid as Of: 2025-07-22\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 432 ---\nComponent: SAP AI Core\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Generative AI hub\nDescription: This initial orchestration endpoint is deprecated and is scheduled for decommissioning on October 31, 2026. Following that date, the endpoint will no longer be available. We recommend that you create new orchestration workflows using version 2, and that you migrate existing workflows from version 1 to version 2. To use version 2, you'll need to update your endpoint from /completion to /v2/completion and modify your existing payloads. For more information, see SAP Note Orchestration Workflow V2 and  3634540 .\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: Deprecated\nType: Announcement\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-07-21\nValid as Of: 2025-07-21\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 433 ---\nComponent: SAP AI Core\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Generative AI hub\nDescription: New models are supported, including Nova Premier from AWS Bedrock.For more information, see SAP Note 3437766 .\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Announcement\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-07-21\nValid as Of: 2025-07-21\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 434 ---\nComponent: SAP Advanced Financial Closing\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Consistency Check Adjustment\nDescription: As previously announced, the consistency check now issues an error message instead of a warning if it detects an empty user group in a task list template.Remember  An error causes the consistency check to fail, which in turn prevents you from generating task lists from the affected template.  More information:  How to Perform Checks on Templates  App affected:  Manage Closing Task Lists  Action: If you haven't done so yet, ensure that you don't have empty user groups. Pay special attention to the warning messages that were issued for empty user groups since the last release, and address the changes required.  For information about how to run a consistency check, see How to Perform Checks on Templates.\nAction: Required\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Finance\nLatest Revision: 2025-07-07\nValid as Of: 2025-07-20\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 435 ---\nComponent: SAP Advanced Financial Closing\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Additional File Types Allowed for Attachments\nDescription: You can now also submit attachments of the file types XLSM and CSV.  More information:  Allowed File Types for Attachments  Apps affected:  Manage Closing Task Lists  Process Closing Tasks  \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Finance\nLatest Revision: 2025-07-07\nValid as Of: 2025-07-20\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 436 ---\nComponent: SAP Advanced Financial Closing\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Information on Details Pages\nDescription: Some information that was previously displayed in the body of the detail pages for task lists, folders, and tasks has now been relocated to the header of the respective pages for better orientation.  App affected:  Manage Closing Task Lists\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Finance\nLatest Revision: 2025-07-07\nValid as Of: 2025-07-20\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 437 ---\nComponent: Decentralized Identity Verification\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Addition of DCP-Holder Protocol Support\nDescription: The new DCP-Holder protocol now supports the credential offer flow.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-01-01\nValid as Of: 2025-07-17\nVersion: 3.11\n\n--- Record 438 ---\nComponent: Decentralized Identity Verification\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Automated Creation of Credential Requests\nDescription: A holder can now configure an automatic creation of credential offers for selected issuers of a credential type.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-01-01\nValid as Of: 2025-07-17\nVersion: 3.11\n\n--- Record 439 ---\nComponent: Decentralized Identity Verification\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Automated Credential Request Creation Following Credential Offers\nDescription: You can now use a service that automatically creates credential requests when you receive a credential offer, provided you have configured automation for the credential offer flow.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 202"], "parameters": {"model": "text-embedding-3-small"}}, "key": "embeddings_f091a67952e71987d40c7130c83e55f40d71cf1ff3ecb13fe74e31d7af70625a_v2"}